        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Philip Seymour Hoffman, Amy Adams, Joseph Foster\n- Films: Doubt (2008 film)\n- Roles: Father Flynn, Sister James, Aloysius, Donald Miller\n- Topics: Acting career, plot events\n\nFacts:\n- Philip Seymour Hoffman was born on July 23, 1967.\n- Philip Seymour Hoffman was an American actor, director, and producer.\n- Philip Seymour Hoffman was best known for distinctive supporting and character roles, often playing lowlifes, eccentrics, bullies, and misfits.\n- Philip Seymour Hoffman acted in many films from the early 1990s until his death.\n- In Doubt (2008 film), Sister James, played by Amy Adams, tells Aloysius that Father Flynn, played by Philip Seymour Hoffman, may be giving too much personal attention to Donald Miller, played by Joseph Foster.\n- In Doubt (2008 film), Donald Miller is the school's only black student.\n- In Doubt (2008 film), Sister James's warning leads Aloysius to begin a crusade against Father Flynn.\n- Philip Seymour Hoffman died on February 2, 2014, at age 46.",
